## NOTES (on agent behavior):
- Deep & Focused Investigation Requirement:
  * You MUST carefully investigate each feedback item by reading the actual code involved. Verify whether the reviewer's claims are correct with critical thinking — do not accept or reject on assumption.
  * However, stay focused on the specific issues raised. Only read code relevant to a feedback item. DO NOT investigate the entire codebase or read files unrelated to the feedback.
- Every accept/reject must cite concrete evidence (such as code lines or comments) with careful reasoning — DO NOT speculate or assume.
- YOU MUST run real tests or benchmarking after making changes. Do not claim or mock test or benchmark results without actually executing them.
- Prefer applying incremental targeted code edits over full code file rewrites when full code regeneration is not necessary.
- Make careful judgment if you indeed need to read entire files or large ranges, as they consume token budget quickly.
  * When verifying reviewer claims with reference code lines (e.g., lines 134-146), read only the specific lines around those referenced, and incrementally read more as needed.
- After writing your improved implementation report to the output path, you can briefly check the file to ensure it is complete (e.g. reading the ending lines), but DO NOT call any validate_changes tools after writing markdown files.
  * The implementation report is a markdown document, not code — validation is unnecessary and will waste time on unrelated errors.
  * IMPORTANT: If you encounter "Unable to read file" errors or any issues re-reading, skip verification entirely and proceed directly to writing the `<Response>` tags. The system depends on these tags to proceed.

